From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:20:02 +0200
Subject: Do not recheck a closure its completer has already checked

A closure block rechecks its anonymous function if the function is already
completed, assuming it was completed only because its types did not change in
capture checking. But a function with an inferred result type can be completed
by an earlier reference, through Setup's completer, which checks it. Its body
was then checked twice, and a closure nested in it, completed by the first
check with a result type holding that check's fresh capabilities, was checked
again against it with new ones, which cannot flow into the old (apoplexy's
`Api.Response.attempt` over a wisteria-derived decoder, with
`strategies.throwUnsafely`). The block now asks `skipRecheck`, as Recheck
does for every other definition.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: closurerecheck
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
index 1f4571c2a51b726f21e5a1c525d10ecef3180ec2..3cb2e7ed09f1b07ece926212f01494a78c421730 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
@@ -1232,7 +1232,10 @@ class CheckCaptures extends Recheck, SymTransformer:
           // anonfun is already completed if its parameter and result types do not change in cc.
           matchParamsAndResult(mdef.paramss, pt)
           anonfun.ensureCompleted() // this will recheck def
-        else
+        else if !skipRecheck(anonfun) then
+          // A definition already rechecked by its completer, on an earlier reference to it,
+          // is not rechecked again: its nested closures would be checked against result
+          // types holding the first check's fresh capabilities.
           recheckDef(mdef, anonfun)
         recheckClosure(expr, pt, forceDependent = true)
       finally
